#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9ecbd28c-9d5a-5802-8792-6ba97651ecd2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Corrector Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56fd02dd-f41d-53f9-a8be-f314fb176330" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339679} {:answer/id #uuid "c103bcf0-a1f0-57e1-9d0c-aa462137be1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{51}{128}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c103bcf0-a1f0-57e1-9d0c-aa462137be1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{51}{128}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339680} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c8dfebf-0aa3-5aa7-aa76-46ada1311bd1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a05b817-7281-5b3e-b53f-298a444d088c" :question/math-academy-id "q-329336" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x-2y+\\frac{3}{2},\\,y(1)=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the $2$-step Adams-Bashforth-Moulton method. Given that the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{2},$ and that one preliminary step has already been computed using the Runge-Kutta method, complete the second row of the table below.\n\n*Hint: The corrector equation of the two-step Adams-Bashforth-Moulton method is defined as*\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{12}(5{y}_{p}^{′}+8{y}^{′}-{y}_{-1}^{′})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\n*where ${y}_{p}$ denotes the predictor at the current step, and ${y}_{-1}^{′}$ is the estimated slope at the previous point.* \n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $\\frac{9}{16}$ |\n| $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{17}{16}$ | $\\frac{7}{8}$ | $\\frac{9}{32}$ | $\\frac{43}{32}$ | $\\frac{13}{16}$ | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe $2$-step Adams-Bashforth-Moulton (ABM2) method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Predictor} & : & Δ{y}_{p} & =\\frac{1}{2}(3{y}^{′}-{y}_{-1}^{′})\\cdot Δx, \\\\ \\text{Corrector} & : & Δy & =\\frac{1}{12}(5{y}_{p}^{′}+8{y}^{′}-{y}_{-1}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}^{′}=f(x,y)$ is the estimated slope at the current point $(x,y),$\n\n- ${y}_{-1}^{′}=f({x}_{-1},{y}_{-1})$ is the estimated slope at the previous point (${x}_{-1},{y}_{-1}),$ and\n\n- ${y}_{p}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})$ is the estimated slope at the predicted new point $({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})=(x+Δx,y+Δ{y}_{p}).$\n\nLooking at the partially filled table, we note the following:\n\n- From the second row, the slope at the current point $(x,y)=(\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{17}{16})$ is ${y}^{′}=\\frac{7}{8}.$\n\n- From the first row, the slope at the previous point $({x}_{-1},{y}_{-1})=(1,\\frac{1}{2})$ is ${y}_{-1}^{′}=\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\n- From the second row, the slope at the predicted new point $({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})$ is ${y}_{p}^{′}=\\frac{13}{16}.$\n\nNow, we compute $Δy$ using the corrector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{12}(5{y}_{p}^{′}+8{y}^{′}-{y}_{-1}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(5\\cdot \\frac{13}{16}+8\\cdot \\frac{7}{8}-\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}\\cdot \\frac{153}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{51}{128}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed row is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $\\frac{9}{16}$ |\n| $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{17}{16}$ | $\\frac{7}{8}$ | $\\frac{9}{32}$ | $\\frac{43}{32}$ | $\\frac{13}{16}$ | $\\frac{51}{128}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f5aefa9-a83c-5203-8b73-c96b5f7df6bf" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Row of a Table Using the ABM 2-Step Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9022cf3e-c94a-5087-be0a-b158f9b85523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11)/(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220248} {:answer/id #uuid "de057609-20bd-5f38-8ad0-3453656a9bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13)/(6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220249} {:answer/id #uuid "43d65a4b-000f-5252-a714-3a10bae99928" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11)/(6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43d65a4b-000f-5252-a714-3a10bae99928" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11)/(6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220250} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d337712-49cc-556d-9bc6-248e675ac5ee" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220247} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f858349-f30b-58f1-88e9-af5534e4edf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10)/(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220252} {:answer/id #uuid "e2331ffa-f916-547c-a819-308f4134543d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8)/(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220253} {:answer/id #uuid "6d786c4e-0b6f-5d84-8ea7-43bd2bb2cc87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4)/(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f858349-f30b-58f1-88e9-af5534e4edf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10)/(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220252} :answer-field/id #uuid "01fd9a1f-c1ec-58b7-b0ac-f104828681b2" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 175921862